{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/rebuild-control.log'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Linking related questions: the build design (D694; for council review before code)\n     2\t\n     3\tAlex chose A (D694): a chosen reading link leaves filing alone; new matching and judging versions open for linking, both opening\n     4\torders; the July test after the council passes the $0 proof. This document is the AGENTS §2 design: the exact texts, the four tables,\n     5\tthe versioning. Nothing here is built yet. The consensus it implements is `RESULT.md` (council R).\n     6\t\n     7\t## 0. Versions\n     8\t\n     9\t- **New configuration `poc/config/poc-v119.json`:** poc-v118 with two changes and nothing else: `matching.engine` `jev-links` (a new\n    10\t  engine name; the matching model, prompt name and every other setting unchanged) and `rejudging.prompt_version` `judging-v8`.\n    11\t- **`judging-v8.txt` is a byte copy of `judging-v7.txt`.** The prompt text does not change; only the code-built dependency block does\n    12\t  (section 3). So a request for a question with no dependency is byte-equal under v7 and v8, and replays from the archive.\n    13\t- **Jev requests that exist today are unchanged** (`jev.request_for` holds the model, state and questions only). The new questions are\n    14\t  new requests in a separate job.\n    15\t- poc-v118 stays the product and the control; its code paths are unchanged (`engine == 'jev'` and `judging-v7` render as today).\n    16\t  `tests/test_frozen_questions_and_judgement.py` stays green: no pinned file or pinned code-written question changes; new\n    17\t  pins are added for the new question texts and judging-v8's file.\n    18\t\n    19\t## 1. Selection: two new Jev questions per pair (engine `jev-links` only)\n    20\t\n    21\tAsked **after** the candidate's final outcome is known (after Jev's relations and the collision judge), only for a candidate whose\n    22\toutcome is `new` or `succession`, against each thesis on its list (`listed`: its search list plus the item's shown questions, the\n    23\tsame list its relation questions used) except its own target, and against the other candidates of the same answer that open. One job\n    24\tper candidate: its `candidate_state` and, per pair, two questions.\n    25\t\n    26\t```\n    27\tREADS = {\n    28\t \"candidate_reads_thesis\": \"the CANDIDATE's answer should be judged with the THESIS's current conclusion in view: the THESIS bounds or drives it (a part read against its whole; an outcome read against an event or quantity it depends on)\",\n    29\t \"thesis_reads_candidate\": \"the THESIS's answer should be judged with the CANDIDATE's current conclusion in view, for the same reasons the other way round\",\n    30\t \"neither\": \"neither answer bounds or drives the other, or they ask the same quantity; sharing a company, industry or topic is not enough\"}\n    31\tinstructions: \"Should one of these two questions be judged with the other's current conclusion in view? Use only the supplied text. THESIS:\\n\" + thesis_text\n    32\t\n    33\tSIGN = {\n    34\t \"together\": \"a higher answer (or yes) to one makes a higher answer (or yes) to the other more likely\",\n    35\t \"opposite\": \"a higher answer (or yes) to one makes a lower answer (or no) to the other more likely\",\n    36\t \"no_clear_sign\": \"the supplied text does not show which way one moves the other\"}\n    37\tinstructions: \"If the THESIS's answer were higher (or yes), which way would the CANDIDATE's answer move? Use only the supplied text. THESIS:\\n\" + thesis_text\n    38\t```\n    39\t\n    40\tSources: PRD 06 (\"B depending on A means B reads A's conclusion\"), D51 (chosen in the matching step), D537 and council R (a part\n    41\treads its whole), D368 item 4 (an outcome reads its driver), judging-v7 line 4 (\"a part cannot exceed its whole\"). The examples\n    42\tname no company or industry (AGENTS §6).\n    43\t\n    44\t**Accepted links**, by code, at threshold 0.5 (Jev's `THRESHOLD`):\n    45\t- direction `candidate_reads_thesis` or `thesis_reads_candidate` at ≥ 0.5 and the sign `together` or `opposite` at ≥ 0.5;\n    46\t- the label is decidable (section 2); otherwise no link, with a note \"link X→Y not written: <reason>\" in the candidate's `reason`;\n    47\t- an asset question reading a theme is not written (note: \"themes reach every asset question through the theme block, D191, D195\");\n    48\t- at most one link per pair: if both directions pass the threshold, the higher probability wins.\n    49\t\n    50\tThe answer shape: each candidate in the Jev answer gains `dependencies` (the existing field: `{view_id, wait_chain_view_id: '',\n    51\twait_year: '', direction}` for \"the candidate reads the thesis\") and a new field `readers` (`[{view_id, direction}]`: \"the shown thesis\n    52\treads the candidate\"). `matching.check` validates `dependencies` as today (shown, not itself, no circle among the answer's candidates)\n    53\tand `readers` the same way (shown, open, not the candidate's own target); a refusal there fails the article, so jev_matching builds\n    54\tonly links that pass these checks (they are identity checks it can make before answering).\n    55\t\n    56\t## 2. The label (code)\n    57\t\n    58\tThe matcher's sign and the two ladders decide it. `ladder_direction(rungs)` gives +1 (values rise from the first rung to the last),\n    59\t−1 (they fall) or None.\n    60\t- **Asset reader R reading T:** R's favourable end is the end whose label is \"Strongly bullish\" (the first or the last rung; any other\n    61\t  label set: undecidable). R's favourable end is high if it is the end where R's values are high. T's end favourable to R: if `together`,\n    62\t  T's high end when R's favourable end is high, else T's low end; if `opposite`, the reverse. The label is `first_is_bullish` when\n    63\t  that end is T's first rung, else `last_is_bullish`.\n    64\t- **Theme reader R reading T:** `same` when (`together`) equals (R and T run the same way), else `opposite`.\n    65\t- Undecidable when either direction is None or the label set does not mark R's ends: no link, with a note.\n    66\t- The label is computed on the rungs as stored after writing (a successor's ladder is oriented like its predecessor,\n    67\t  `writing.oriented_like`), so for a candidate that opens as a successor the oriented rungs are used.\n    68\t\n    69\tWorked case (old-2 07-10): R = v9 (rung 1 \"Strongly bullish\", at least $450B: values fall, favourable end high), T = v14 (values fall),\n    70\t`together` → T's high end = its first rung → `first_is_bullish` (the label the probe used).\n    71\t\n    72\t## 3. What the reader is shown (judging-v8; code in `judging._lines_english`)\n    73\t\n    74\tFor each dependency, in place of today's single line:\n    75\t```\n    76\t- v14 (open; first_is_bullish) How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?: now rung 3 Neutral, judged 2026-07-12\n    77\t    Comparison point stated by that judgement: <its stored reference>\n    78\t    The system's forecast for it (our own judgement, not evidence): <its stored implied_outcome>\n    79\t    Reasons (excerpt): <its reasons, first 600 characters>\n    80\t```\n    81\tNot yet judged: \"now not judged yet\" and no further lines; waiting and \"historical only\" print as today. `store.current_state`\n    82\treturns `reference`, `implied_outcome` and `publication_day` as well (its other readers use only rung and reasons). Under judging-v7\n    83\tthe block is byte-equal to today's.\n    84\t\n    85\t## 4. Writing and filing\n    86\t\n    87\t- **Store:** `dependencies` gains a column `kind` (`ensure_writable_columns` adds it; old rows read `''`). The new path writes\n    88\t  `kind = 'reads'`. Seed rows and every row written before keep `''` and are read exactly as today.\n    89\t- **Filing:** `store.direct_parents` (filing's only reader of the table, via `extraction.shown_views` → `narrowest_links`) skips rows\n    90\t  with `kind = 'reads'` (D694 (a): D265 applies to a stated hierarchy only). Every other reader (judging order, the block, citations,\n    91\t  queues, the circle check, service, bundle, search, research context, idea route) reads `reads` rows as dependencies, as today.\n    92\t- **The candidate reads a thesis:** written by `writing._write` step 2 as today (the cycle check, duplicates within the write), with\n    93\t  `kind = 'reads'`.\n    94\t- **A shown thesis reads the candidate (new):** after the new view exists, for each `readers` entry: if the pair (reader, new view) with\n    95\t  the same label exists, nothing; with another label, refused; if `would_cycle(reader, new view)`, refused; else written with the\n    96\t  article's seq and `kind = 'reads'`, and the reader is added to the article's `changed` set, so it is judged in that day's round after\n    97\t  the new view. Each refusal is a note in the article's `written` record (\"link R→T refused: circle\" / \"conflicting label\").\n    98\t- **The circle rule.** PRD 06 says refuse and ask the model to correct, with persistent cycles following normal failure handling. Jev\n    99\t  answers the same request the same way, so a correction cannot change it; failing the article would stop the day on every replay. So\n   100\t  the link is refused and recorded, and the article proceeds. **A departure from PRD 06's wording for this engine, put to the council.**\n   101\t\n   102\t## 5. Table 1: state × event (a pair of questions R, T)\n   103\t\n   104\t| Event | No link | Link R reads T (`reads`) |\n   105\t|---|---|---|\n   106\t| T opens; R exists and is shown; Jev answers `thesis_reads_candidate` with a sign and a decidable label | the link is written at the article's seq in its commit; R added to `changed`; that evening T is judged first, then R reads T's conclusion | the same label: nothing; another label: refused, noted |\n   107\t| R opens; T exists; Jev answers `candidate_reads_thesis` | written with R in step 2 as today; R judged that evening after T if T is judged | n/a (R is new) |\n   108\t| both open in the same article | the same, within the answer; a circle among the answer's candidates is refused by `matching.check`, so jev_matching never proposes one (it keeps the higher-probability direction) | n/a |\n   109\t| the link would close a circle through stored links | refused, noted; the article proceeds | as left |\n   110\t| Jev's answer is below threshold, no sign, undecidable label, asset reading a theme | nothing written; a note in the candidate's reason | as left |\n   111\t| T's conclusion changes in a round | nothing | R queued once in the same round, after T (`queued_by_change`) |\n   112\t| T's conclusion is unchanged; R has no new evidence | nothing | R not judged (as today) |\n   113\t| R has no evidence in force | not judged (D59) | not judged |\n   114\t| T closes | nothing | R reads T's last conclusion marked \"closed\" (as today); a successor of T is not followed (no resolution writer for links; none is needed for one fiscal period) |\n   115\t| R closes | nothing | R is not judged; the row stays as history |\n   116\t| a crash after the article's commit / midway through a round | n/a | the link is in the commit or absent; a resumed round rebuilds its queue (`queued_by_ledger`) |\n   117\t| a resumed article (crash before its commit) | n/a | the Jev answers replay from the archive; the same links are proposed and written once |\n   118\t| a later article proposes the same pair | n/a | only when one of the two is that article's candidate: no (the pair exists only between a candidate and a shown thesis); two already open questions are not linked in this version |\n   119\t| a later run under poc-v118 on the same store | nothing | `reads` rows are read by judging-v7 as dependencies with today's line (a v118 run never writes them; mixing is not a supported use) |\n   120\t\n   121\t## 6. Table 2: value × reader\n   122\t\n   123\t| Value written | Readers |\n   124\t|---|---|\n   125\t| `dependencies` row, `kind='reads'` | `judging.topological`, `upstream`, `build_prompt`, `check_answer`, `queued_by_change`, `queued_by_ledger`, `store.would_cycle`, `dependants_of`; `service.dependencies`/`dependants`, `bundle`, `search` records, `research_context`, the idea route: all read it as \"R depends on T\", which is its meaning. `store.direct_parents` (filing) skips it. |\n   126\t| `kind=''` (all existing rows) | every reader as today |\n   127\t| the Jev answer's `readers` and `dependencies`, the notes | `match_records.decisions_json`; `matching.check`; `writing._write`; the `written` record's notes |\n   128\t| the reader added to `changed` | `round.changed_views_of_day` → `judge_day` |\n   129\t| `current_state`'s new fields | the judging-v8 block only |\n   130\t\n   131\t## 7. Table 3: new path × old checks\n   132\t\n   133\t| Check | Under poc-v119 |\n   134\t|---|---|\n   135\t| every stored poc-v118 request replays byte-equal | requests without a dependency are equal (v8 = v7 text; existing Jev jobs unchanged); proved by the July control rebuild under v118 (`rebuild_control.py`) and a v119 replay of 07-01..07-09 with no link written yet (to be proved) |\n   136\t| `cites_views` only names shown dependencies | unchanged: the block and the check read the same rows |\n   137\t| dependencies judged first; a dependant reads this round's conclusion | unchanged on `reads` rows |\n   138\t| filing: D265 on seed rows | unchanged (`kind=''`); `reads` rows skipped: replay filing over old-2's 106 shared items with a link present: no link removed |\n   139\t| `matching.check` refusals fail the article | jev_matching proposes only checkable links |\n   140\t| frozen-piece tests | green; new pins for `READS`, `SIGN` texts and `judging-v8.txt` |\n   141\t| D59, the theme block (D195) | unchanged |\n   142\t\n   143\t## 8. Table 4: prior decisions\n   144\t\n   145\t| Decision | Here |\n   146\t|---|---|\n   147\t| D51, D368 item 2 | the matching step chooses (a Jev question) |\n   148\t| D191 point 2 | an existing question gains a link when the read question opens; two already open questions: not in this version |\n   149\t| D191, D195 | no asset→theme link |\n   150\t| D207, D265, D694 (a) | a `reads` link moves no statement |\n   151\t| D260 | the reader sees the read judgement's reference and implied outcome |\n   152\t| D354, D359 | new versions, poc-v118 untouched |\n   153\t| PRD 06 (cycles) | refused and recorded, not retried (section 4): for the council |\n   154\t| D542's items | circle through a waiting link: Jev links never wait; closing: as table 1; theme twice: no asset→theme link; historical readers: no resolution rows are written by this path, so the reverse-lookup gaps Codex found are not reached; `last_end`: none |\n   155\t\n   156\t## 9. Tests (written with the code; each names its row)\n   157\t\n   158\t1. The label mapping on the worked case and its three mirrors (sign opposite; R ascending; T ascending), and undecidable cases.\n   159\t2. jev_matching under `jev-links` with a fake Jev transport: `thesis_reads_candidate` → `readers`; `candidate_reads_thesis` →\n   160\t   `dependencies`; below threshold, no sign, asset→theme, both directions → one link; under `jev` no new question is asked.\n   161\t3. The writer: an existing reader gains a `reads` row, is in `changed`; duplicate, conflict and circle are refused with notes; the\n   162\t   article commits.\n   163\t4. Filing: `direct_parents` skips `reads` rows; a seed-style row still narrows (the existing test stays green).\n   164\t5. judging-v8's block on a stored-like ledger; judging-v7's block byte-equal to today's.\n   165\t6. Mutants for 2, 3 and 4 (the new question asked under `jev`; a `reads` row narrowing filing; the reader not queued).\n     1\t2026-07-01 | items  13 extracted  13 merged  0 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence   5 new views  3 judged   3 changed   3 closed 0 | open views 3 | day $0.00 total $0.00 calls 0\n     2\t2026-07-02 | items  19 extracted  17 merged  2 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence  23 new views  1 judged   3 changed   3 closed 0 | open views 4 | day $0.00 total $0.00 calls 0\n     3\t2026-07-03 | items  10 extracted   9 merged  1 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence   4 new views  0 judged   2 changed   0 closed 0 | open views 4 | day $0.00 total $0.00 calls 0\n     4\t2026-07-04 | items   6 extracted   5 merged  1 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence   7 new views  2 judged   6 changed   5 closed 0 | open views 6 | day $0.00 total $0.00 calls 0\n     5\t2026-07-05 | items  10 extracted   7 merged  3 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence  13 new views  2 judged   8 changed   7 closed 0 | open views 8 | day $0.00 total $0.00 calls 0\n     6\t2026-07-06 | items  29 extracted  25 merged  4 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence  51 new views  1 judged   9 changed   7 closed 0 | open views 9 | day $0.00 total $0.00 calls 0\n     7\t2026-07-07 | items  22 extracted  22 merged  0 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence  31 new views  0 judged   9 changed   6 closed 0 | open views 9 | day $0.00 total $0.00 calls 0\n     8\t2026-07-08 | items  27 extracted  26 merged  1 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence  31 new views  3 judged  10 changed   8 closed 0 | open views 12 | day $0.00 total $0.00 calls 0\n     9\t2026-07-09 | items  24 extracted  23 merged  1 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence  29 new views  1 judged   5 changed   3 closed 0 | open views 13 | day $0.00 total $0.00 calls 0\n    10\ttotals: {'items': 160, 'extracted': 147, 'skipped': 0, 'merged': 13, 'not_processed': 0, 'returned': 0, 'failed': 0, 'evidence': 194, 'new_views': 13, 'judged': 55, 'changed': 42, 'closed': 0}\n    11\tlast completed seq at 2026-07-09 147\n    12\tviews: rebuilt 13 stored 13 equal\n    13\tview_keys: rebuilt 13 stored 13 equal\n    14\tevidence: rebuilt 194 stored 194 equal\n    15\tevidence_links: rebuilt 232 stored 232 equal\n    16\tjudgements: rebuilt 55 stored 55 equal\n    17\tdependencies: rebuilt 0 stored 0 equal\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
