{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files poc/config | rg 'v11[89]'\nrg -n 'cfg\\\\.matching\\\\.engine|v8' docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/round4-brief.md\nnl -ba clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py | sed -n '20,128p'\nnl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '90,120p'\"","aggregated_output":"poc/config/poc-v118-from-v7.json\npoc/config/poc-v118-idea.json\npoc/config/poc-v118-from-v1.json\npoc/config/poc-v118-from-v2.json\npoc/config/poc-v118.json\npoc/config/poc-v118-from-v9.json\n22:6. Versioning (section 0): `judging-v8.txt` as a byte copy of v7 and the engine name `jev-links`. Acceptable under D354/D359, and does\n    20\t\"\"\"\n    21\timport argparse\n    22\timport contextlib\n    23\timport fcntl\n    24\timport io\n    25\timport json\n    26\timport math\n    27\timport os\n    28\timport sys\n    29\timport threading\n    30\timport time\n    31\timport types\n    32\timport urllib.error\n    33\timport urllib.request\n    34\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    35\t\n    36\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    37\tROOT = HERE.parents[1]\n    38\tsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / 'src'))\n    39\tfrom hivemind import config, jev, model, parallel_day, replay, universe  # noqa: E402\n    40\t\n    41\tCLIENT_ERRORS = {400, 401, 403, 404}\n    42\t# How many reservations the calling thread holds and has not settled (the interception proofs read it). One object per process, kept in\n    43\t# sys.modules, because each component loads this file under its own module object.\n    44\t_MARK = sys.modules.setdefault('hivemind_shared_ledger_live_mark', types.ModuleType('hivemind_shared_ledger_live_mark'))\n    45\tif not hasattr(_MARK, 'local'):\n    46\t    _MARK.local = threading.local()\n    47\t_LIVE = _MARK.local\n    48\t\n    49\t\n    50\tdef holds_live_reservation():\n    51\t    \"\"\"Whether the calling thread holds a reservation it has not yet settled (WIRING-DESIGN.md §B2, the interception trap).\"\"\"\n    52\t    return getattr(_LIVE, 'depth', 0) > 0\n    53\t\n    54\t\n    55\tdef lock_is_free(lock_path):\n    56\t    \"\"\"Whether no process holds the lock file: a shared, non-blocking flock succeeds only when no exclusive holder is alive.\"\"\"\n    57\t    try:\n    58\t        with open(lock_path, 'a') as handle:\n    59\t            try:\n    60\t                fcntl.flock(handle, fcntl.LOCK_SH | fcntl.LOCK_NB)\n    61\t            except BlockingIOError:\n    62\t                return False\n    63\t            fcntl.flock(handle, fcntl.LOCK_UN)\n    64\t            return True\n    65\t    except OSError:\n    66\t        return True\n    67\t\n    68\t\n    69\tdef install_stop_gate(ledger):\n    70\t    \"\"\"Process-wide: every `urllib.request.urlopen` call, a helper's internal retry included, first reads the shared ledger. When it is\n    71\t    stopped, or when a registered launcher's lock is free (that launcher died without removing its entry: the gate then stops the\n    72\t    ledger), the call is refused as HTTP 403 (no component retries a 403) and nothing is sent. An attempt whose read came before a stop\n    73\t    was written may finish; one that reads after it is refused. Returns a function that removes the gate.\"\"\"\n    74\t    original = urllib.request.urlopen\n    75\t\n    76\t    def gated(request, *arguments, **keywords):\n    77\t        state = ledger.stop_if_a_launcher_is_gone()\n    78\t        if state.get('stopped'):\n    79\t            raise urllib.error.HTTPError(getattr(request, 'full_url', str(request)), 403,\n    80\t                                         f\"the shared ledger is stopped ({state.get('stop_reason')}): not sent\", {},\n    81\t                                         io.BytesIO(b'{\"error\": {\"type\": \"shared_ledger_stopped\"}}'))\n    82\t        return original(request, *arguments, **keywords)\n    83\t    urllib.request.urlopen = gated\n    84\t\n    85\t    def remove():\n    86\t        if urllib.request.urlopen is gated:\n    87\t            urllib.request.urlopen = original\n    88\t    return remove\n    89\t\n    90\t\n    91\tclass SharedLedger:\n    92\t    \"\"\"One JSON ledger for every run under a ceiling, guarded by an exclusive file lock (processes and threads). The first refused\n    93\t    reservation, or an explicit `stop`, persists `stopped` with its reason under the lock: every later reservation, in any thread or\n    94\t    process, is refused (WIRING-DESIGN.md §B2, D448).\"\"\"\n    95\t\n    96\t    def __init__(self, path):\n    97\t        self.path = Path(path)\n    98\t        self.lock_path = self.path.with_suffix('.lock')\n    99\t        self.attempts_path = self.path.with_suffix('.attempts.jsonl')   # one line per settled or refused attempt: the measurement record\n   100\t\n   101\t    def _note(self, entry):\n   102\t        \"\"\"Append one attempt line (the process, the call kind, the amounts, the tokens when reported, the moment) for per-component\n   103\t        spend and timing. Written only after the ledger's state is saved, and best-effort: a failed append never blocks a stop, a charge\n   104\t        or an overrun. A crash between the two writes leaves the lines short of the ledger, never ahead of it; the tally reports the gap\n   105\t        as unaccounted. One short append, so concurrent lines do not interleave.\"\"\"\n   106\t        line = json.dumps(dict(entry, pid=os.getpid(), at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%z'))) + '\\n'\n   107\t        try:\n   108\t            with open(self.attempts_path, 'a') as handle:\n   109\t                handle.write(line)\n   110\t        except OSError:\n   111\t            pass\n   112\t\n   113\t    @contextlib.contextmanager\n   114\t    def _locked(self):\n   115\t        with open(self.lock_path, 'a+') as lock:\n   116\t            fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\n   117\t            try:\n   118\t                state = json.loads(self.path.read_text())\n   119\t                yield state\n   120\t                temporary = self.path.with_suffix('.tmp')\n   121\t                temporary.write_text(json.dumps(state, indent=1))\n   122\t                os.replace(temporary, self.path)          # a reader never sees a half-written ledger\n   123\t            finally:\n   124\t                fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_UN)\n   125\t\n   126\t    @staticmethod\n   127\t    def init(path, ceiling):\n   128\t        Path(path).write_text(json.dumps({'ceiling': ceiling, 'spent': 0.0, 'reserved': 0.0, 'overrun': False, 'refused': 0, 'attempts': 0,\n    90\t\n    91\t## 2. Before writing code: design\n    92\t\n    93\tCode written before the thinking costs rounds of review. A design holds these tables before code and before any review; a blank cell\n    94\tmeans it is not ready:\n    95\t\n    96\t1. **State × event**, for work that spans more than one step, run or day: every state against every event it can meet (success,\n    97\t   refusal, a refused retry, an external failure, a crash midway, work still in flight when a run ends, a later run on a later date,\n    98\t   configuration changed in between, an input corrected while waiting, another writer of the same data, two scopes at once), including\n    99\t   the work before its first step and after its terminal outcome. Each cell names the transition, what is written, and the date every\n   100\t   read and write uses.\n   101\t2. **Value × reader.** Every value a change writes, against every reader of it (found by searching the field) and every input source the\n   102\t   value can come from. A rule over a kind of data lists every writer of that kind. A change to how often something fires is counted\n   103\t   against every reader of its output.\n   104\t3. **New path × old checks.** For a new input, derived value, mode or changed data shape: every check the old path passes, and whether\n   105\t   the new one meets it. A changed shape re-derives every check written for the old one.\n   106\t4. **Prior decisions.** The decisions searched for the mechanism by name; any decision that rejected or bounded it is quoted in the\n   107\t   design and in the question to Alex.\n   108\t\n   109\t- A contract over text or shapes states the closed set of what passes (a full match); anything else fails or is not judged. Enumerate\n   110\t  the accepted set against every context and reader it meets before the first edit.\n   111\t- **Code owns identity, never importance.** Before building a closed list, enum or gate, write which decision it takes from the model\n   112\t  and whether that decision is identity (\"are these the same thing?\") or judgement (\"does this matter?\"); build only the identity part.\n   113\t  A list of what matters is at most a hint shown to the model (Alex, 2026-10-25: \"你这个做法难道不是非常的限死吗？永远都是一堆财务指标，真正的观点呢？\").\n   114\t- **No case-fitted fix.** A hand list, a special path or a rule fitted to the case in view fixes that case and breaks the next. First ask\n   115\t  whether the judge had the material and the definition it needed, and whether a typed field is missing; run the proposal against the\n   116\t  existing tests and the gold for a counter-example before building (D167: \"我不要 hardcode 解法 it's premature optimization, not general root fix\").\n   117\t- A blind review measures the tables. A serious finding they do not hold shows a missing dimension: add it and walk every row again,\n   118\t  never answer the finding alone. Code starts when the review finds nothing serious. A design whose core contract is still open is a\n   119\t  question, not something to build.\n   120\t- A foundation's acceptance carries a size and speed budget from its first control, not only correctness.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 PYTHONPATH=src python3 -c '\nfrom hivemind.extraction import check_bounds, check_ladder\nfrom hivemind.views.matching import ladder_direction\nfrom hivemind.vocabulary import ASSET_LABELS\nbands = [(400,None),(0,100),(200,400),(100,200),(None,0)]\nrungs = [dict(label=label,condition=\\\"numeric band\\\",lo=lo,hi=hi) for label,(lo,hi) in zip(ASSET_LABELS,bands)]\nprint(\\\"shuffled\\\",check_ladder(rungs,\\\"asset\\\"),check_bounds(rungs),ladder_direction(rungs))\nevents=[dict(label=\\\"Yes\\\",condition=\\\"At least 5 permits\\\"),dict(label=\\\"No\\\",condition=\\\"At most 4 permits\\\")]\nprint(\\\"event\\\",check_ladder(events,\\\"asset\\\"),check_bounds(events),ladder_direction(events))\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
