{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"agent_message","text":"I checked the exact July 10 matcher input. It contains the $393B company estimate and the reported 92% Data Center share, which support the intended direction. The design still leaves gaps in how the writer handles several proposed links together and how the July test rules out cached answers."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT READY. The July inputs support the intended link, but the design leaves the writer and the test harness with decisions they cannot safely infer.** On July 10, the matcher sees the $393B company projection and a report that Data Center accounted for 92% of Q1 sales. That supports Data Center reading total revenue. It does not show that any higher total forecast automatically raises the segment forecast. [July selection record](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/selection-census.md:59)\n\n## Blockers\n\n**1. Tables 1–3 use “final identity” before the code has resolved it.** The Jev candidate loop produces provisional outcomes. `matching.check` can still turn a proposed opening into a merge or skip, and `identity.batch_plan` can join two same-item candidates into one stored question. `thesis_text` also requires a stored ID, so it cannot render a same-item candidate. Specify the sequence: validate destinations, resolve aliases and prospective successor ladders, render each eligible pair once, then validate and write the resulting links. Give `readers` an explicit checked representation and retain the per-pair IDs actually shown. The current `Checked` type has no `readers` field. [Design §1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:19) · [Jev renderer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:56) · [Checked type and destination checks](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/matching.py:259) · [Identity coalescing](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/identity.py:74)\n\n**2. Tables 1, 3 and 4 disagree on cycle handling.** One direction per pair still permits A reading B, B reading C and C reading A. A new question can also close a cycle through existing links. The old check walks candidate dependencies, while the writer checks stored links one insertion at a time. As drafted, the same invalid graph could fail the article or lose whichever link happened to be inserted last. Validate the complete proposed graph on resolved IDs, with one owner rechecking the result at the write boundary. Specify how duplicate and conflicting labels are recorded. The current `written` record keeps only the first 20 notes, so it cannot be the sole record of refusals. [Design §4 and Table 1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:85) · [Candidate cycle check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/matching.py:377) · [Writer cycle check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:175) · [Note limit](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/round.py:153)\n\n**Require the PRD 06 correction path.** Jev replaying an identical request proves that an identical retry is useless. It gives no reason to rule out a correction request that names the conflicting links and asks for a legal answer. Specify that request and the outcome if the correction fails. If the intended policy is instead to discard a cycling link and commit the article, obtain an explicit amendment. D694 did not authorize that departure. [PRD 06](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/06-views.md:133) · [Current Jev retry branch](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/round.py:35) · [D694](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10439)\n\n**3. Tables 1 and 4 narrow the agreed lifecycle without settling the boundary.** The proposal suppresses every asset-to-theme link, accepts event wording in `SIGN`, and then assumes targets never need event succession. The council agreed that a linked theme already in the theme block appears once, and that a closed event becomes historical background until a successor takes over. A blanket theme ban also covers closed or unjudged themes, which the theme block already omits. In the other direction, a theme reading an asset can make the asset run first and miss that theme’s new answer. Keep the agreed cases and specify which routes render, cite and queue them, or explicitly approve a narrower endpoint set. For awaited links, “this engine never writes a wait” is sufficient only if writable input stores are also guaranteed to contain no waits. The current writer resolves old waits whenever it opens a question. Put that admission boundary in the table and exercise it. [Design Table 4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:143) · [Council R agreement](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/RESULT.md:29) · [Theme rendering](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:76) · [Ready order](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:306) · [Waiting resolver](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:49)\n\n**4. The July harness needs an explicit archive, outcome and spending contract.** The $0 log establishes the starting state at sequence 147. Clone it for each sequence and ensure the archive lookup itself cannot return a stored answer for either target question. A transport guard alone runs too late. Dry-run July 10–12 with labelled fixed responses, including a different first-day answer, to prove the next request uses that sequence’s own history. Verify the snapshot fields that drive the replay, including ladders, judgement citations and change flags, and closure state. The current comparison checks selected columns. [Rebuild log](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/rebuild-control.log:10) · [Snapshot comparison](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/rebuild_control.py:37) · [Archive lookup before transport](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:251)\n\nSpecify what happens if real matching picks a legitimate additional link. For example, the July 10 request also shows the stand-alone CPU question. A link there could change an unrelated judge request. Preserve the real selection, stop on the unexpected archive miss, and record the result under a predeclared rule. An absent or incorrect intended link still counts as a selection miss. The linked version would also ask new Jev questions before July 10 if replayed from July 1. Start the comparison from the rebuilt v118 prefix and prove any v119 prefix compatibility with explicit fixed selector answers. Finally, reserve against the **shared $0.15 ceiling before each provider attempt**, including judge retries and Jev calls. `replay.run` checks spend after items and before the day’s judging calls. Keep the agreed cap-stop outcome of inconclusive. [Selector scope](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:19) · [July test plan](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/RESULT.md:49) · [Replay budget check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/replay.py:108) · [Prior probe reservation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/probe.py:100)\n\n## High-severity contract gaps\n\n**5. Rewrite `READS` and `SIGN` around the chosen reader.** For old-2, the expected `READS` answer is `thesis_reads_candidate`. `SIGN` then asks the wrong conditional: it changes Data Center and asks what happens to total revenue, although the chosen reader is Data Center. Ask about the effect of the **read question’s** outcome on the **reading question**. Under a stated continuing-mix assumption, `together` is defensible for July. A bound alone can be loosened without changing the most likely answer, so `no_clear_sign` needs to cover that case. This leaves relevance and sign with the model. Code should check identity, allowed answers and whether the result maps to a label. Specify whether Jev’s returned `choice` or the rounded probabilities decide ties. Two displayed scores can both be `0.50`. [Design question texts and threshold](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:26) · [Jev choice validation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/jev.py:52)\n\nThe wording is industry-neutral, but the audit is incomplete. Source the driver case to PRD 06’s dependency examples. D368 item 4 concerns preset arrows. Qualify “same quantity” by period and scope, so an earlier-period figure can still be relevant. PRD 06 excludes completed events from dependency selection. The blanket exclusion of a candidate’s predecessor needs a source or should be removed. Add the cross-industry examples required by AGENTS §6, including both directions and no link, and show how the same-item question is rendered. [PRD 06](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/06-views.md:114) · [AGENTS §6](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:194)\n\n**6. The label arithmetic works on the worked case and mirrors, within a narrower set of ladders.** From the worked case, changing only the sign, only the reader’s numerical order while keeping its bullish end first, or only the target’s order each gives `last_is_bullish`. The theme formula works when both numerical orders are established. “Strongly bullish” marks a unique favourable end for a five-rung asset ladder with exactly the canonical labels or their reverse. Two-rung asset ladders can pass with other labels. Also, `ladder_direction` can infer order from prose, and the extraction bounds check sorts the intervals before checking them. I verified at $0 that a ladder with shuffled middle intervals passes both extraction checks while `ladder_direction` still says it is descending. Define the supported set using typed bounds in actual rung order and a unique favourable end, with an explicit undecidable outcome for everything else. Apply that rule after successor orientation. [Asset ladder checks](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:411) · [Bounds check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:493) · [Order inference](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/matching.py:72) · [Successor orientation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:72)\n\n**7. Table 1 needs the failure and restart cases at the actual boundaries.** Add selector transport or schema failure, refused correction, a stale plan at write time, work still in flight, and resume with changed configuration or changed input. State what a second writer to the same store can do, and how separate scopes are isolated. The write savepoint protects the item’s writes. Sequence allocation happens earlier, and the parallel manifest’s input and configuration checks do not cover serial replay. Also add the comparison-point-only change case from round 3. The round queues on the judge’s `changed` flag, but the previous-conclusion block does not explicitly show the previous comparison point. Demonstrate what the judge can compare and how a material change reaches its reader without claiming the old request is byte-identical if that input changes. [State table](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:102) · [Sequence allocation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/dispatch.py:49) · [Write transaction](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:112) · [Parallel manifest](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/parallel_day.py:68) · [Previous conclusion and queue](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:156)\n\n## Compatibility and versioning\n\n- **`current_state` can return the two fields without changing existing v7 output.** I found no v7 caller that emits the entire dictionary. The judge and `show_views.py` select known fields. `publication_day` is already returned. Specify how v8 displays missing legacy values and format the new text so it cannot be mistaken for a block header or citation line. Table 2 also needs to account for `research_context` returning dependency rows via `SELECT *`, which would expose the new `kind` column. Use an explicit projection if the historical response shape is to stay stable. Specify the `kind` migration default so legacy rows retain their filing behaviour. [State query](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:230) · [Judging renderer and citations](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:137) · [CLI reader](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/show_views.py:25) · [Research context](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/research_context.py:34)\n- **`judging-v8.txt` as a byte copy and `jev-links` are acceptable under D694.** Enumerate the supported version combinations and define what happens when a v118 writer opens a v119 store. “Mixing is not supported” needs an entry-point outcome. Today the config rejects `jev-links`, the match round would route it to the generative matcher, and the replay and parallel runner have their own exact checks for `jev`. Cover all of those and exercise the default CLI path. Keep the v7 pins. Add pins for the complete new Jev question builders, the v8 file and schema, and a request-level control for the code-built block and the no-link byte equality. Hashing the prompt file alone cannot catch changes to the block. [Config engine validation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/config.py:46) · [Matcher dispatch](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/round.py:35) · [CLI worker defaults](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/replay.py:82) · [Parallel runner](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/parallel_day.py:92) · [Frozen tests](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_frozen_questions_and_judgement.py:14)\n\nBefore build, revise the four tables to specify final identities and one checked graph, settle the lifecycle and cycle-correction rules, close the request and ladder contracts, and write the July archive and budget rules. Add decisive $0 tests for those reachable cases and return the design for review. **NOT READY TO BUILD.**"}}
